('RFA-F028','medium','Public holonomy carriers bypass shape and inverse admission','DiscreteConnection and ExactMatrix expose mutable/deserializable dimensions/data/maps. Reverse transport can change without changing forward state/hash; malformed1x1empty matrix can reach direct indexing in supposedly fallible arithmetic. CellComplex consumers other than guarded cochain_matrices also trust public index maps.',[a.ev(c,40,47),a.ev(c,112,125),a.ev(c,218,225),a.ev(m,243,266),a.ev(m,338,370),a.ev(l,66,90)],'Builder-valid objects retain their checked invariants until mutation; cochain_matrices explicitly reconstructs and rejects malformed carriers, so the finding does not apply to that guarded path.'),
('RFA-F029','medium','Content hashes use noninjective endpoint encodings','Valid endpoint pairs(a->b,c)and(a,b->c)serialize to the same edge text a->b->c. With identical matrix values, connection digests coincide; graph digests also coincide when both use the same four-vertex set and their distinct single edge.',[a.ev(c,218,225),a.ev(g,233,264),a.ev(g,69,114)],'This is an encoding collision, not a cryptographic SHA256collision. It uses only valid builder identifiers and does not require public-field forgery.'),
('RFA-F030','medium','Self-loop admission breaks pair-keyed inversion semantics','set_connection(u,u,[2]) stores forward2 and reverse1/2 under the same key; get_step(u,u)always selects2. Thus the stated U(v,u)=U(u,v)^-1 law fails for an admitted loop. Graph permits loops, counts them once despite incoming+outgoing degree wording, and Laplacian skips them entirely.',[a.ev(c,60,108),a.ev(c,112,125),a.ev(g,86,114),a.ev(g,180,192),a.ev(l,70,84)],'Edge-indexed gauge-fixing API remains separately pending and may handle orientations correctly. This finding concerns the vertex-pair API; rejecting loops or carrying an orientation would avoid the ambiguity.'),
('RFA-F031','medium','Laplacian construction does not establish its PSD or graph contract','compute accepts arbitrary invertible transport and arbitrary signed weights. U=2 yields[[1,-2],[-1/2,1]], which is not Hermitian; identity transport with weight-1 yields a negative quadratic form. It also builds nonzero blocks for connection edges absent from CellComplex, invalidating the unconditional trace2d|E|statement.',[a.ev(l,41,99),a.ev(l,102,145)],'For loop-free matching simple graphs, unitary transports and symmetric nonnegative real weights, the resulting reversed-transport matrix is PSD. Those required conditions are not enforced by this constructor.'),
('RFA-F032','high','Laplacian block orientation conflicts with connection gauge action','Connection transports map u to v and transform g(v)U(u,v)g(u)^-1, but Laplacian block(u,v)stores-U(u,v)instead of reverse transport. Starting from identity edge and rational orthogonal gauges g(a)=I,g(b)=J=[[0,-1],[1,0]], the constructed transformedL differs from G L G^-1 and sends the transported parallel section(1,0,0,1)to(2,0,0,2).',[a.ev(c,185,215),a.ev(h,66,88),a.ev(l,70,84),a.ev(l,116,128)],'Countercontrol uses valid unitary rational2x2transports, positive unitweight and a single graph edge. It is not due to malformed fields or failure of scalar laws.'),
('RFA-F033','medium','Perturbation bound trusts nonnegative weights without checking them','A four-cycle with alternating weights+1,-1has all weighted diagonal degrees0and a nonzero Hermitian Laplacian. Its certificate reports operator_norm_bound0for epsilon2. Changing every unittransportI to-I gives nonzero Hermitian delta with absolute row sum4, contradicting that numerical bound.',[a.ev(l,196,217),a.ev(l,220,290)],'The control violates the documented nonnegative-weight convention, which compute/certificate do not enforce. For admitted nonnegativeweights and Hermitian perturbations, the written Weyl-Gershgorin bound is appropriate. The unperturbed gap is supplied, not independently measured.'),
('RFA-F034','medium','Face flatness and arbitrary loop products do not certify pure gauge or homology pairing','is_flat returns true on every face-free graph regardless of cycle holonomy. A two-cycle graph with noncommuting unipotent transports has a commutator loop with zero H1class but nonidentity transport; cycle_homology_pairing returns that raw matrix despite its H1pairing label.',[a.ev(h,127,152)],'Local curvature flatness is a valid narrower predicate. Global pure gauge needs trivial generator holonomies; homology descent additionally needs suitable abelian/flat hypotheses. No claim against the explicitly qualified Bianchi routine.'),
('RFA-F035','medium','Nested built-in Gaussian scalar is not a field and rank hides inversion refusal','GaussianRational<T> implements ExactScalar for every ExactScalar T, including GaussianRational<BigRational>. The nonzero outerelement(inner i,inner1)has norm i²+1=0and refuses inversion; rank of its1x1matrix silently returns0because exact_inv errors are discarded.',[a.ev(m,94,115),a.ev(m,215,240),a.ev(m,665,688)],'Ordinary QandQ(i)overQare unaffected. Nested built-in instantiation shows the trait bound is insufficient for advertised field elimination; a domain restriction or propagated error is needed.'),
('RFA-F036','medium','Several operation-limit parameters are not enforced on the mathematical work','curvature_commutator names its limits argument _limits and uses unbounded matmul. Path holonomy uses try_identity/matmul without max_dimension or contraction limits; matmul_with_limits itself checks only result rows/columns, admitting arbitrarily wide inner dimension under a small dimension limit.',[a.ev(r,14,33),a.ev(h,72,88),a.ev(m,382,397)],'Checked integer products and allocation failure handling remain useful. This is a declared budget boundary gap, not evidence that ordinary small calculations are wrong.'),
